    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, our offensive core is headlined by **Josh Naylor** (76.25) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (76.91), who both benefit immensely from facing a soft matchup against Imai and Pallante, respectively. **Vinnie Pasquantino** (76.21) remains a locked-in start, as his ability to capitalize on the high xERA of Fedde aligns perfectly with his strong platoon advantage. **James Wood** (70.66) is also a high-priority play; despite Singer\u2019s presence on the mound, Wood\u2019s position atop the order provides the volume necessary to hunt runs and steals, keeping his floor comfortably above the 70-point threshold despite a challenging SP profile.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Trevor Story** (45.19), who narrowly missed the cut. While his park factors are favorable, he was pushed out by the higher efficiency scores of our middle-infield and outfield depth; furthermore, the prospect of facing the elite arm of Wheeler created too much risk for a player currently operating at a marginal efficiency level. Conversely, we are keeping a close eye on **Brice Turang** (50.39) and **Dalton Rushing** (56.56). Their scores are pending official lineup confirmation, and both carry inherent risk due to their lower-tier spots in the order and the potential for a negative variance in plate appearances if the projected batting order shifts downward.\n\nRisk management remains a priority today, particularly regarding our sprint-dependent players. **Corbin Carroll** (60.21) earns a spot despite a tough matchup against Gore, as his dynamic speed remains too valuable to ignore in our league settings, even when the platoon splits aren't ideal. We are proceeding with caution regarding **Mickey Moniak** (54.09), who draws a difficult assignment against the high-velocity Skenes. While the platoon advantage keeps him marginally startable, the elite nature of the opposing pitcher necessitates a lower efficiency score than the rest of our outfield cohort. Stay vigilant on the **Dalton Rushing** and **Brice Turang** lineup postings, as any drastic drop in their batting order could necessitate a late-cycle roster adjustment.",
